 "CONCLUSION": "The set-redundancy hypothesis is CONFIRMED as a diagnostic (missed golds are reliably more novel than top5 FPs: Qwen cohend -0.52, support cohend -0.67, query-conditioned paired diff significant on both dev splits, ~80% of queries) BUT it is NOT CONVERTIBLE into a top-5 gain. Deterministic MMR (C10a) ties C8c (+0.0004 NDCG@5, not significant); a from-scratch pointwise selector (C10b) collapses; a relevance-preserving per-step NDCG ranker with a C8c-seeded rank-1 (C10b2) is still significantly worse (-0.0126 NDCG@5), hurting the very 2/3+-gold tail it targeted. Root cause: novelty separates missed-golds from FPs ON AVERAGE, but at the per-candidate decision boundary the novel population is dominated by non-gold distractors, so acting on it (greedy or MMR) swaps in more noise than evidence, and greedy set-selection additionally forfeits the joint listwise optimization C8c already performs. STANDING TOP-5 POLICY REMAINS C8c. The remaining ~0.0208 top-50 oracle gap (3+-gold tail) needs a genuinely NEW discriminative signal or a larger scope, not set-aware reselection of the current pool. Returned BEFORE official VAL."
}